From 8e5a840478ab8f7ab4d059f4bd3b17d73f17231e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 13:58:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] media: rkvdec: leave clock enables to runtime PM

devm_clk_bulk_get_all_enabled() leaves one enable reference on every
decoder clock until unbind. Runtime resume enables the same clocks
again and runtime suspend drops only that second reference, so
autosuspend never actually gates them.

Acquire the clocks without enabling them and keep runtime PM as the
sole owner of their prepare/enable state.

Fixes: 6a846f7d72c7 ("media: rkvdec: Enable all clocks without naming them")
Signed-off-by: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
index 28451ce68c9c8..054eb8a366df1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
@@ -1879,7 +1879,7 @@ static int rkvdec_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	ret = devm_clk_bulk_get_all_enabled(&pdev->dev, &rkvdec->clocks);
+	ret = devm_clk_bulk_get_all(&pdev->dev, &rkvdec->clocks);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
